  "releaseNotes": "Core:\n      - Added smart span casting for RequestModel, ResponseModel, and buffers, enabling direct use of ReadOnlySpan<byte/char> with zero‑copy behavior.\n      - Removed per‑session ResponseModel from all HTTP/HTTPS protocols; responses are now pooled and created only when needed.\n      - Simplified session APIs by consolidating send methods and removing redundant overloads, keeping the interface minimal and consistent.\n      - Improved naming and structure of core methods for clearer intent and better long‑term maintainability.\n      - Refined WebSocket upgrade flow to use pooled response objects safely without shared‑state mutation.\n      - Reduced allocations across the entire pipeline and improved throughput under high concurrency.",
